187 0 obj
<<
/Dest [ 102 0 R /Fit ] /Next 188 0 R /Parent 139 0 R /Prev 185 0 R /Title (Description: sshd in OpenSSH before 10.6p2 on Linux, when musl libc is used without PAM, lacks a workaround for a password authentication bypass \(related to misinterpretation of whether a string is intended to be a password hash\). For some configurations of accounts, any password between 256 and 1024 characters succeeds. An example of a platform using musl libc without PAM is Alpine Linux.)
>>
endobj
